      "notes": "Equations — a sample deck authored for edot slides. CC0 1.0 / public domain dedication (see third_party/slide-examples/LICENSE). Doubles as an import-fidelity test fixture.\n\nNOTE ON FIDELITY: real PowerPoint equations use OMML (Office Math Markup Language) inside a:txBody. The edot PPTX exporter does NOT emit OMML — it has no math run support. This deck therefore represents every formula as plain Unicode text (∑ ∫ √ ∂ ∇, Greek letters, super/subscripts, unicode fractions), which round-trips losslessly as text but will not become a native equation object in PowerPoint."
